{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:10:09Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 61, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GZR5curMKqfGajqTvV6Wox", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/spec.md", "content": "# Spec: Show how many tasks are left\n\nTaiga #10\n\n## Workspace check\n\n`git status` is clean on `feature/tp-10/show-how-many-tasks-are`; no foreign\nwork to relocate.\n\n## Triage\n\n**Feature.** Net-new: a visible count of open and done tasks. Frontend-only \u2014\nthe full task list is already fetched into `App.jsx` state on every load and\nafter every mutation, so the counts are a derived view, not new data.\n\n## Goal\n\nAs someone using the tracker, I want to see at a glance how many tasks are\nopen and how many are done, without counting rows myself.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. **Given** the task list has loaded, **when** it renders, **then** the page\n   shows an open-task count and a done-task count, each a plain integer\n   derived from the full task list (not the filtered/visible subset \u2014 see\n   Open Questions).\n2. **Given** zero tasks exist, **when** the page renders, **then** it shows\n   `0` for both open and done, not blank or hidden.\n3. **Given** exactly one task exists, **when** the count for that bucket is\n   `1`, **then** the copy reads grammatically singular (e.g. \"1 task\", not\n   \"1 tasks\"); every other count (0, 2, 3, ...) reads plural. This holds\n   independently for the open count and the done count.\n4. **Given** a task is added, **when** the add succeeds, **then** the open\n   count increases by 1 and the done count is unchanged, with no page reload.\n5. **Given** an open task is marked done, **when** that completes, **then**\n   the open count decreases by 1 and the done count increases by 1.\n6. **Given** a task is deleted, **when** that completes, **then** the count\n   for whichever bucket it belonged to (open or done) decreases by 1; the\n   other bucket is unchanged.\n7. **Given** \"Clear completed\" removes N done tasks, **when** that completes,\n   **then** the done count decreases by N and the open count is unchanged.\n8. **Given** the list is still loading (before the first fetch resolves),\n   **when** the page renders, **then** no count is shown (matches the\n   existing `loading` gate in `App.jsx:60-71`) rather than showing a stale\n   or momentarily-wrong `0`.\n9. **Given** a fetch error occurs, **when** `error` is set, **then** the\n   existing error message still renders as it does today; the count is not\n   required to be more informative than the current error UI.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No backend/API change. `GET /api/tasks` already returns the full list;\n  counts are computed client-side. No new endpoint, no change to\n  `backend/app/main.py`, `models.py`, or `store.py`.\n- No per-priority breakdown (e.g. \"2 high-priority open\"). Just open vs.\n  done totals.\n- The count is not persisted anywhere; it's a pure render-time derivation\n  from existing `tasks` state, same pattern already used for\n  `completedCount` at `frontend/src/App.jsx:38`.\n- Not changing what `TaskFilter` or `ClearCompleted` do today.\n\n## Affected areas\n\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 already computes `completedCount` (line 38) the\n  same way this needs to compute an open count; both derive from `tasks`,\n  not `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`, per acceptance criterion 1. New display\n  wired in here, likely near the toolbar (`list-toolbar` div, lines 56-59) or\n  the `<h1>` \u2014 exact placement is ux-designer's call.\n- New component file under `frontend/src/components/` (naming/shape is\n  ux-designer's/developer's call) \u2014 sibling pattern to inspect:\n  `frontend/src/components/ClearCompleted.jsx`, which already takes a\n  `count` prop and does its own pluralization-free label (\"Clear completed\n  (N)\"); this feature additionally needs singular/plural grammar, which\n  nothing existing does yet.\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styling for the new element, plain CSS per\n  project convention.\n- No backend files. No `frontend/src/api.js` change \u2014 no new request.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Zero tasks total (criterion 2).\n- Exactly one task, in either bucket (criterion 3) \u2014 explicitly called out\n  by the requester.\n- All tasks open / all tasks done (one bucket at 0, still must read as\n  plural \"0 tasks\", not suppressed or hidden).\n- Loading state before first fetch resolves (criterion 8).\n- Rapid successive mutations \u2014 already handled by the existing `run()` \u2192\n  `refresh()` cycle in `App.jsx:40-49`, which re-fetches and re-renders\n  after every mutation; the count just needs to derive from `tasks` on every\n  render rather than tracking its own state, so it can't drift.\n- Fetch error mid-session (criterion 9) \u2014 count should not crash or show\n  `NaN`; while `error` is set, `tasks` retains its last-known value (state\n  is not cleared on error in the current `refresh()`), so the count keeps\n  showing the last-known-good numbers, consistent with how the rest of the\n  UI already behaves on error.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Does the count follow the active filter, or always show the true\n  total?** Assumption: always the true total (all tasks), independent of\n  `TaskFilter`'s `all`/`open`/`done` selection. Reasoning: the request says\n  \"stay correct as I add, complete and delete tasks\" and asks how many are\n  \"left\" and \"done\" \u2014 that's about actual task state, not about what's\n  currently scrolled into view. If filtered to \"done\" and the open count\n  read `0` just because open tasks are hidden, that would misreport reality.\n  Proceeding on this assumption; flag if wrong before design starts.\n- **Exact wording/placement.** Left to ux-designer, per specced grammar rule\n  in criterion 3 and general placement guidance above (toolbar area).\n"}, "session_id": "af69a51a-65ab-43c5-a509-abdf1673915b"}}
